        "answer": {
          "text": "Thank you for coming. I will begin my pitch with the timeline. By the end of March, we will have signed the lease, and we are getting the permit approved. Meanwhile, Leo is having the sign made, and this time next month we will be putting up the shelves. By the first of June, we will have opened the doors. The main risk is a fall in demand in winter. Should demand fall, we will use our cash reserve and offer home repairs. I understand your concern about the forecast, but let me reassure you: fifty repairs a month is realistic because two competitors are already busy and there is a niche for fast repairs.",
